From: NapiLab <info@napilab.ru>
Subject: [PATCH] mrm: close the ring on a returning MRP_Test after a LinkChange open

The kernel reports a returning MRP_Test only while its ring state is not
closed. When a MRC's MRP_LinkDown opens the ring before the test frames time
out, the kernel never reports loss of continuity (it does that only in the
closed state), both ports keep loc false and every later "test returned"
report is dropped as a repeat: the MRM stays in CHK_RO with the ring closed
and the secondary forwarding until the next local link change.

Seen on NAPI-Switch (MRM) with software MRCs: every break of a link next to
a MRC that the MRC itself reports left the ring in CHK_RO.

diff --git a/state_machine.c b/state_machine.c
index 0c41cdb..5527da4 100644
--- a/state_machine.c
+++ b/state_machine.c
@@ -2296,7 +2296,17 @@ void mrp_port_ring_open(struct mrp_port *p, bool loc)
 	    mrp->mra_support != true)
 		goto out;
 
-	if (p->loc == loc)
+	/* The kernel reports a returning MRP_Test (loc false) only while the
+	 * ring state it holds is not closed, i.e. while this MRM is not in
+	 * CHK_RC, so such a report always means the ring closed. Do not drop it
+	 * as a repeat: when the ring was opened by a MRP_LinkChange from a MRC
+	 * before the test frames timed out, the kernel never reported loc true
+	 * (it does that only in the closed state), both ports still have loc
+	 * false and the MRM would stay in CHK_RO with the ring closed.
+	 */
+	if (p->loc == loc &&
+	    (loc || mrp->ring_role != BR_MRP_RING_ROLE_MRM ||
+	     mrp->mrm_state == MRP_MRM_STATE_CHK_RC))
 		goto out;
 
 	p->loc = loc;
